# Do not add blanket negations here.
#
# This block used to read:
#     !README.md
#     !docs/**
#     !src/**
#     !database/**
#     !configs/**
#
# None of those paths is ignored by any rule above, so the negations bought
# nothing -- but a negation re-includes everything it matches. `!src/**` therefore
# defeated the `__pycache__/` and `*.py[cod]` rules at the top of this file and 8
# compiled .pyc files were committed (AUDIT.md F-20). `!database/**` did the same
# to the database volume directories ignored above, so postgres/neo4j/qdrant data
# was one `git add -A` away from the repository.
#
# If a negation is ever genuinely needed, scope it to the single path that needs
# it and add a comment saying which rule above it is meant to override.

# Belt and braces: bytecode is never tracked, wherever it lives.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]


# Editable-install metadata
*.egg-info/

# M3 evaluation: per-item workflow artifacts (raw retrieval, context, prompt,
# answer, evaluation JSON for each item). ~12MB of intermediates. The run_*.json
# and baseline_*.json summaries carry everything the metrics are computed from --
# routes, evidence samples, answer text, scores, token counts -- so the artifact
# directories are reproducible output, not source.
tests/eval/results/*/
